{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1126312-failing-to-pay-for-permanent-attribute-boosts-so-what","id":1126312,"title":"Failing to pay for Permanent Attribute Boosts; so what?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-08T08:09:45-07:00","id":1126312,"title":"Failing to pay for Permanent Attribute Boosts; so what?","content":"If you use Life to give yourself a permanent Strength boost from 4 to 5, but fail to pay for it with EXP (half the usual cost) you get a backlash from reality as your body rejects this altered Pattern. You take one unsoakable level of lethal damage each day.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> So?<br /> <br /> For a Vampire, rising with a wound every night is a big deal, since it doubles how much blood you need to subsist. Mages don't need to spend anything to heal themselves, and healing from Bruised is never going to be vulgar (I drink a coffee and perk up from grey and sick looking to perfectly healthy, no one is questioning the possibility of this recovery). Healing that one point each day isn't going to be hard to pull off for someone with the Life necessary to make such transformations.<br /> <br /> The only reason I can see for investing the EXP is that you can't take TOO much damage. Say you wanted to boost your Strength from 1 to 5; the rejection is going to be 4 points of lethal each night, which is a serious problem. Firstly your recovery when you wake up is Vulgar; a Hypothetical Observer would find it very strange that you could recover from a pretty badly wounded state on a daily basis. Secondly it would preclude boosting absolutely anything else, since you're so close to the edge as it is. But all this means is that the player would pay for Strength 2, 3 and possibly 4 and leave the 5th level to the Transformation (Scientists hate him! Meet the Verbena who got swole in just ten minutes!), taking that one point of damage each night as a small cost for the pinnacle of human strength.<br /> <br /> Am I missing anything? Any players or STs have experience with refusing to pay for such transformations in full?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T09:59:35-07:00","id":1126338,"title":"","content":"As a ST, I would make that damage aggravated (the pattern rejects it, should be agg Dmg anyways) and now your mage has a problem. He needs a point of quintessence to heal his wound every day. Limit healing as a whole. Some editions of Mage claim a pattern can only be healed once per scene. And the last part: Paying the Exp is what makes that effect permanent. Have an antagonist npc ban that spell and that mage is back to normal.<br /> There's lots of things a ST can do, especially in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13530-queen-nihil","name":"Queen Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13530_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:56:46-07:00","id":1126371,"title":"","content":"At times, damage to the pattern cannot be healed with magick.<br /> For example, when you use the Heart's Blood rote to exchange health levels for Quintessence - essentially tearing at your pattern and turning it into said quintessence - it is explicitely stated that you cannot heal the damage with magick - only with time and mundane means.<br /> <br /> So you can simply go along that road if you want; The lethal damage from pattern bleeding is the same kind of damage as with Heart's blood - parts of the pattern tearing - and can also only healed by time. Which means that mage is now permanently stuck with at least a level of lethal damage...which takes a day to heal, if I recall right off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> <br /> So far so good, you gain a level a day, you heal a level a day. No biggie, right?<br /> <br /> But, you know what's worse? If they get that level of damage while they are already even slightly hurt, because then they are stuck with a non-magick-healable level of damage further down the chart in healing time, and the downward spiral begins as they gain pattern damage levels faster than they can naturally heal them, unless they revert their pattern...<br /> <br /> Food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-08-2017, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:55:42-07:00","id":1126422,"title":"","content":"As Queen Hihil implied: it's &quot;pattern damage&quot;, direct pattern damage it's always Aggravated. You need Quint to heal Aggravated.<br /> <br /> It's worth to note that you can avoid the damage from &quot;pattern bleeding&quot; by spending Quintessence, thus it's feasible to have the enhancement for a few days without losing Healt if you have a Node or something.<br /> <br /> Also, I think somewhere I read that patern bleeding does what Ambros\u00eda sugested (it's unhealable), albeit I think that's too much. Needing to expend the Quint to heal it's enough punishment, since it's what you require to avoid the damage in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you want the enhancement to last longer than a few days without XP, make it permanet for a point of Permadox, the bleeding it's only required for non permanent changes, as far as I'm aware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-08-2017, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T15:34:25-07:00","id":1126477,"title":"","content":"I could easily be wrong, but I'm not sure that permadox would stop the pattern bleed. And permadox, in my recollection, only comes into play when boosting an attribute beyond 5 (and for this situation, is only 'permanent' in the sense that backlashing it won't cause it to go away, but ending the effect will cause it to go away). Apologies, but I only vaguely remember stringing together some sparse statements about this in M20 and How Do you Do That? (possibly also flipping through Revised and Second Edition) to arrive at a rough understanding.<br /> <br /> I think it's fair to demand the quintessence per day or suffer the appropriate level of damage (whether it be lethal or aggravated is something I would rely on others for at this time). The permadox I would kick in for any modifications above 5 (perhaps one 'permadox' per attribute above 5), which is involved in every backlash roll that occurs and yet does not deplete until the effect ends.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind too that this effect is potentially increasing the difficulty of performing other effects (especially if one likes to stack a bunch of different effects on). If the player can't come up with a paradigm-appropriate explanation for why they are increasing their Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina in one effect, then it's possible that they are running 3 effects (meaning a +1 difficulty to all Arete rolls or +2 if they slap on one more effect for four ongoing effects total, etc.).<br /> <br /> I think being willing to pay the half-experience point cost for the attribute is not a bad bargain. That said, another fairly simply option is to do a brief rite (5 minutes or so, 1-2 rolls, 5 successes) each day for a day-long duration boost of up to 3 attribute points. Avoid the pattern bleed and maintain flexibility on how many effects the character runs (as well as how the points are allocated).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T17:57:14-07:00","id":1126524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could easily be wrong, but I'm not sure that permadox would stop the pattern bleed. And permadox, in my recollection, only comes into play when boosting an attribute beyond 5 (and for this situation, is only 'permanent' in the sense that backlashing it won't cause it to go away, but ending the effect will cause it to go away). Apologies, but I only vaguely remember stringing together some sparse statements about this in M20 and How Do you Do That? (possibly also flipping through Revised and Second Edition) to arrive at a rough understanding. </div> </div> </div>That rule has never been terribly clear nor consistent between editions: In HDYDT, for instance, would give you the reason but with a few caveats:<br /> <br /> Permadox it's <b>only </b>gained for vulgar modifications (it doesn't say that Atributes over 5 are Vulgar, though, on the contrary, the book states that this depends if the modification it's evident or not, super Intelligence may be more subtle, and thus, Coincident, than superhuman Appearance).<br /> <br /> And the &quot;pay experience or suffer Patern Bleeding&quot; it's only gained if the modification it's Permanent, but you get no Pattern Bleeding if you only make the spell last...say...six months (Hey, it's not permanent!). The damage it's <b>Lethal </b>and impossible to resist,but can be healed as normal (or at least nothing suggests otherwise, and thus these rules do not adress the problems of 11twiggins)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Book</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If the mage wants to make certain \u201cmodifications\u201d permanent,</b> <b>then </b>she needs toeither pay experience points to retain increased Attributes...If the player does not pay the points to retain those Attributes, then the character suffers a Paradox inflicted rotting disease...That rejection process<b> inflicts one lethal health level</b> in damage per day (no soak possible)</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised has, in my opinion,a better rule: In the Life Sphere it's stated that you gain Pattern Bleeding any time you alters your pattern in a way that isn't natural (increasing Atributes or adding unnatural characteristics). Each different change supposes a healt level (they do not specify the type, but pattern damage it's usually Aggravated, and that would adress 11twiggins dilema) you loose each day unless you spend Quintessence, undo the changes, or make them permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-08-2017, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T19:16:07-07:00","id":1126554,"title":"","content":"The above comment is really helpful, thank you!<br /> <br /> I would refer to page 516 in M20, which as far as I can tell suggests that pattern bleeding occurs at a rate of one lethal health level per day for any effect that is &quot;not part of the creature's original Pattern.&quot; I will just paste the block of text:<br /> <br /> &quot;When used to inflict or repair damage, Life deals out aggravated damage because it works directly upon the Patterns of living things. As a result, an organism that has been radically altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern bleeding: an inexorable Quintessence leak that inflicts one level of lethal damage per day. Unless the caster uses Prime magick to refill that Pattern with fresh energy, or alters that Pattern permanently, the damage continues until the subject dies.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","user":"Imperator","date":". 08-09-2017, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:34:51-07:00","id":1126678,"title":"","content":"@ OP: A few more options come to mind. Long exposure to body enhancing magic might result in genetic flaws. As a ST I would ask my player to actually play out how waking up each morning with a level of pattern damage gnaws at the characters long term health, maybe add a few mali, if he fails to play out some consequences. Long term damaging and reweaving of his pattern could screw him up badly. He could lose stamina, gain some rather unhelpfull mutations (again, genetic flaws), become a beacon of rather nasty resonance or whatever. It's mage, your players will find ways to screw the rules, so a ST has to be creative too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13530-queen-nihil","name":"Queen Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13530_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:43:16-07:00","id":1126679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Nihil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1126312-failing-to-pay-for-permanent-attribute-boosts-so-what?p=1126678#post1126678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ OP: A few more options come to mind. Long exposure to body enhancing magic might result in genetic flaws. As a ST I would ask my player to actually play out how waking up each morning with a level of pattern damage gnaws at the characters long term health, maybe add a few mali, if he fails to play out some consequences. Long term damaging and reweaving of his pattern could screw him up badly. He could lose stamina, gain some rather unhelpfull mutations (again, genetic flaws), become a beacon of rather nasty resonance or whatever. It's mage, your players will find ways to screw the rules, so a ST has to be creative too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could just make the daily routine of artificially reinforcing your Pattern drain your Willpower. Insomnia follows. You begin to run low on Willpower, and run the risk of getting in serious trouble if you face mind-bending stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:44:18-07:00","id":1126680,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses! Great ways for an ST to encourage use of EXP ;-)<br /> <br /> Still, great for Life Mages that they can halve the EXP cost of Attributes. if you were trying to increase every Attribute up to 5 that would save you a LOT of EXP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}